/-!
# The situation of [Stacks, Tag 07MZ], and the coefficients it is stated for

[Stacks, Tag 07MZ] ("Complete comparison") concerns a scheme `Y` proper and smooth over the
divided power base `S` itself, rather than over the closed fibre `S₀`, with the crystalline
situation's `X` recovered as `Y ×_S S₀`, and a crystal in quasi-coherent `𝒪_{X/S}`-modules of
**finite type**. This file defines these hypotheses and coefficients.

## The statement of [Stacks, Tag 07MZ]

> Let `p` be a prime number.  Let `(A, I, γ)` be a divided power ring with `A` a Noetherian
> `p`-adically complete ring and `p` nilpotent in `A/I`.  Set `S = Spec(A)` and `S₀ = Spec(A/I)`.
> Let `Y` be a proper smooth scheme over `S` and set `X = Y ×_S S₀`.  Let `ℱ` be a finite type
> crystal in quasi-coherent `𝒪_{X/S}`-modules.  Then
>
> 1. there exists a coherent `𝒪_Y`-module `ℱ_Y` endowed with integrable connection
>    `∇ : ℱ_Y ⟶ ℱ_Y ⊗_{𝒪_Y} Ω_{Y/S}` such that `ℱ_Y/p^eℱ_Y` is the module with connection over
>    `A/p^eA` found in Remark [Stacks, Tag 07MW], and
> 2. we have `RΓ(Cris(X/S), ℱ) = RΓ(Y, ℱ_Y ⊗_{𝒪_Y} Ω^•_{Y/S})` in `D(A)`.

## The hypotheses

Situation [Stacks, Tag 07MF] is `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation` itself.  The further
hypotheses of [Stacks, Tag 07MZ] are the fields of `Situation07MZ`:

| source hypothesis | spelling here |
| --- | --- |
| `S = Spec(A)` | `isAffine`, so that `A = Γ(S, 𝒪_S)` |
| `A` is Noetherian | `isNoetherianRing` on `Γ(S, 𝒪_S)` |
| `A` is `p`-adically complete | `isAdicComplete` for `Ideal.span {p}` |
| `p` is nilpotent in `A/I` | `prime_nilpotent_closedFiber`, nilpotence of `p` in `Γ(S₀, 𝒪_{S₀})` |
| `Y` is a scheme over `S` | `Y` together with `toBase : Y ⟶ S` |
| `Y → S` is proper | `isProper` |
| `Y → S` is smooth | `isSmooth` |
| `X = Y ×_S S₀` | `toY : X ⟶ Y` together with `cartesian` |
| `ℱ` is a finite type crystal in quasi-coherent modules | `IsFiniteTypeQuasicoherentCrystal ℱ` |

The prime `p` is nilpotent in `A/I` but not assumed nilpotent in `A`, so `X ⟶ Y` is a closed
immersion but need not be a thickening, and `(X, Y, γ)` need not be an object of `Cris(X/S)`.

## Main definitions

Everything below lives in the namespace `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite`.

* `IsFiniteTypeQuasicoherentCrystal` — a finite type crystal in quasi-coherent
  `𝒪_{X/S}`-modules, the coefficients of [Stacks, Tag 07MZ].
* `Situation07MZ` — the hypotheses of [Stacks, Tag 07MZ], as data.

## Main results

* `Situation07MZ.isClosedImmersion_toY` — in the situation of [Stacks, Tag 07MZ] the map
  `X ⟶ Y` is a closed immersion.

